@crew mensah
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}, cadet. Mensah, night Watch. If you're up past midnight, I'll see you.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}! Up late? Me too. It's my job, though.   #funny
- {me}. She's quiet tonight. I like her quiet.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}! Good. Walk a deck with me? I could use the company.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Made the Chief laugh twice today. Twice! I'm writing it down.   #funny
? mood:low
- Long night round. Every deck, every door. My feet have opinions.
== near
? time:night
- Good night, Deck 4. That's the whole of my Deck 4 speech.   #funny
? act:gym
- Treadmill's mine at this hour. No leaderboard. No Commander. Bliss.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I walk the whole ship once a night, deck by deck. You learn her sounds.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Getting a laugh out of Holt. It's like fishing. Patience, and the right line.
